<title>CANADA: Canadian Gas Association storage survey - Nov 1.</title>
<headline>Canadian Gas Association storage survey - Nov 1.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Gas Association (CGA) weekly survey of Canadian natural gas in storage in billion cubic feet (bcf):</p>
<p>							 Pct Full  Pct Full</p>
<p>		 11/01/96  10/25/96  Pct Full  Week Ago  Year Ago</p>
<p>East	    218.86    217.52    94.11	93.54     97.40</p>
<p>West	    234.26    237.93    88.45	89.84     79.90</p>
<p>Total Canada  453.12    455.45    91.10	91.57     89.20</p>
<p>East-West division is the Manitoba/Saskatchewan and North Dakota/Minnesota borders.</p>
<p>East capacity 11/01/96: 232.55 bcf, 10/25/96: 232.55 bcf.  </p>
<p>West capacity 11/01/96: 264.84 bcf, 10/25/96: 264.84 bcf.</p>
<p>The Canadian Gas Association survey includes liquefied petroleum gas, all Canadian operators of gas storage and Canadian companies contracting gas storage in the U.S. --Calgary Bureau 403-531-1624</p>
</text>
